## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

**Summary: 14 findings — 8 Critical, 2 High, 4 Medium**

This suite is a textbook **coverage-touching** class. All 10 public methods of `ProductCatalog` are called, producing ~95% line coverage, but **6 of 10 tests have zero assertions** and the remaining 4 use only trivial `IsNotNull` checks. None of the tests verify that the system did the right thing.

---

### 🔴 Critical — False Confidence

#### 1. Systematic Coverage-Touching (entire file)

The suite walks every public method in declaration order with no meaningful verification. This is the single root cause of "95% coverage, bugs in prod."

#### 2. No Assertions — 6 tests (lines 17–21, 31–36, 39–43, 63–66, 68–74, 85–88)

| Test | Line | What's missing |
|------|------|----------------|
| `AddProduct_Works` | 17 | Never verifies product was stored |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | 31 | Never verifies price changed |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | 39 | Never verifies product is gone |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | 63 | Discards return value entirely |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | 68 | Never verifies prices reduced |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` | 85 | Never verifies product was imported |

**Fix example — `AddProduct_Works` → `AddProduct_StoresProduct`:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.IsNotNull(stored);
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
}
```

**Fix example — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` → `ApplyBulkDiscount_ReducesPricesByFraction`:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ApplyBulkDiscount_ReducesPricesByFraction()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 100m));
    _catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);

    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.IsNotNull(updated);
    Assert.AreEqual(90m, updated.Price);
}
```

#### 3. Trivial `IsNotNull` Assertions — 4 tests (lines 23–29, 46–52, 55–60, 77–82)

These assert the return value isn't null but never check **content**. `GetProduct` could return the wrong product; `Search` could return zero results; `ExportToCsv` could emit garbage — all tests would still pass.

| Test | Line | What `IsNotNull` misses |
